# promise: #806
# ⌘Z after Remove Favorite puts the favorite back where it was, as in Arc (asked for on X, GitHub #806). With
# Share Favorites off, Remove Favorite archives the tab; ⌘Z reopened it as a closed tab, at the end of Pinned
# and opened, instead of back in the favorites. The open favorite removed opens again; one that wasn't stays
# closed. A posted ⌘Z reaches the window's key monitor in a background copy (no screen needed).
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=one
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=two
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=three
wait 1
cra://action/favoriteTab
wait 1
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=1&label=start&run=-
expect-log favorite menu start favorites: n=one n=two n=three today: *open: n=three$

# A favorite that isn't open: back in its place, still closed.
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=2&label=removed&run=Remove Favorite
expect-log favorite menu removed favorites: n=one n=three today: *open: n=three$
cra://debug?key=z,6,1048576
wait 1
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=1&label=undone&run=-
expect-log favorite menu undone favorites: n=one n=two n=three today: *open: n=three$

# The open favorite: back in its place and open again.
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=3&label=removed-open&run=Remove Favorite
expect-log favorite menu removed-open favorites: n=one n=two today: *open: -$
cra://debug?key=z,6,1048576
wait 1
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=1&label=undone-open&run=-
expect-log favorite menu undone-open favorites: n=one n=two n=three today: *open: n=three$

# Once: a second ⌘Z reopens nothing more from the favorites.
cra://debug?key=z,6,1048576
wait 1
cra://debug?favoriteMenu=1&label=again&run=-
expect-log favorite menu again favorites: n=one n=two n=three
cra://debug?checkStore=1
